# Internal working documents never belong in this repository, which is public.
# Plans, porting notes, audits, reconnaissance and agent reports live one
# directory up, outside the repo. Only user-facing docs ship here: README,
# LICENSE, NOTICE, THIRD_PARTY and the per-module READMEs.
#
# What may stay at the root is named here, rather than what may not. The
# forbidden-prefix list this replaces did not hold: it said `audit-*.md`, and
# what accumulated was `marketplace-ux-audit.md` — the same word on the other
# end. Twelve internal reports sat in the working tree of a public repository,
# one careless `git add -A` from being published. An allowlist cannot fail that
# way, because a document nobody has vouched for is ignored by default.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/THIRD_PARTY.md

# The same documents, should they ever be written into a subdirectory.
ARCHITETTURA.md
PORTING-*.md
*-REPORT.md
*audit*.md
*review*.md
recon/

# Raw agent and test-run transcripts. Regenerable by definition, and superseded
# the moment they are written: whether a slice passed is recorded by CI, not by
# a captured terminal.
*-red.txt
*-green.txt
verify*.txt
tmp-jobs/

# Not the Windows null device. A POSIX shell redirecting to `nul` creates an
# ordinary file, so this is where stray error output collects unnoticed.
nul

# Workspace-local Oracle/Augur runtime data (CKG, findings ledger).
oracle-data/
